WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
Choose a position that asks as little effort as possible.

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.890
You can sit, stand, or lie down.

3
00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:13.780
If closing your eyes does not feel right, leave them open and let your gaze rest somewhere simple.

4
00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:27.202
Notice that the ground is already meeting you.

5
00:00:28.902 --> 00:00:35.122
Feel one or two places where your body is supported: feet on the floor, the seat beneath you, or the surface under your back.

6
00:00:49.766 --> 00:00:52.586
There is nothing special to make happen.

7
00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.676
Let the next breath arrive in its own shape.

8
00:00:58.376 --> 00:01:00.696
Feel where it is easiest to notice.

9
00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:05.275
Perhaps at the nose, the chest, or the belly.

10
00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:25.899
When attention moves away, that is not a mistake.

11
00:01:27.599 --> 00:01:30.199
The moment you notice is already a moment of returning.

12
00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:35.449
Come back to one point of contact, and then to one ordinary breath.

13
00:01:57.414 --> 00:01:59.994
For a little while, receive each inhale.

14
00:02:01.694 --> 00:02:03.664
Let each exhale finish without pushing it.

15
00:02:05.364 --> 00:02:06.734
Body supported.

16
00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:09.324
Breath moving.

17
00:02:11.024 --> 00:02:13.384
Sounds coming and going.

18
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.520
Now notice the room around you.

19
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.660
Let your eyes take in light and shape if they were lowered.

20
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.500
Feel the next small movement you want to make.

21
00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.060
You have arrived for these few minutes.

22
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.000
Nothing else is required.
